f  all living things line up with garo's  goals garu actually doesn't dismiss him  but asks if that's true what should he  do to which blast suggests that he'll  lead him to another dimension he tells  him to take a look at the effect he's  having on everyone and we see that  almost everyone can't tolerate the  cosmic radiation garu is giving off the  effect is reminiscent of conqueror's  hockey from one piece where the  low-level characters are just taken out  from the get-go of course blast has  resistance to it but he explains the  others will die just from garo being  here now that is quite an insane level  of power blast notices now that garo  does retain some humanity and wonders if  he managed to stave off the full  impartation of god's power if so blast  fears what would happen if god's full  impartation of power was complete blast  is then about to utter some very hype  words literally all we're missing right  now is saitama showing up and getting  serious and we'll get that later in the  chapter 2 but not yet the hype thing  blast says is if garo won't listen to  reason then it'll be a battle of  supremacy between two beings who  manipulate the reality of the cosmos to  decide who is right and who is wrong  we're learning a lot about blast here  including the fact that he understands  the importance of power no matter what  at the end of the day the stronger will  ultimately have the privilege of  choosing who is right aka of making  themselves right might makes right if  you will it's also hype how they're  represented as divine like beings who  can manipulate the reality of the cosmos  and i realize i might be saying hype a  lot in this chapter review but it was a  very hyped chapter although we all know  saitama will beat his opponents in the  end getting to see awaken garo push  blast to his limit would be amazing garo  laughs saying divine power ain't bad at  all just him being around means that  he's finally getting to be the symbol of  fear he always wanted to be he's still  aligned with his goal even if it means  he can't be close to others he finally  proclaims he is that miserable future  disaster level god and yeah i don't  really think anyone can question that  disaster level anymore it makes you  think though how strong is this god  figure himself if he can make others so  powerful bang tries to interfere with  garo but blast tells him to stop since  if he gets closer he'll only die i love  bang's attitude here though he's just  like so what i love that zorro-like  contempt for death all the while garo  contemplates evil how no one needs to  understand it how people are miserable  if they are around it he's tried to  convince himself to finish off bang and  to never see the kid who looks up to him  again it's a recurring idea to shone and  you gotta cut all ties off if you wish  to reach your goal like sasuke and  naruto but as we know people with that  ideology usually get knocked to their  senses sooner or  jenos later in with the headbutt he's in  no condition to fight but he keeps  fighting because he's not affected by  the radiation either nice touch there  since it makes sense that he would be  less effected as a cyborg plus what is  about to happen because of this genos  intervention just makes the chapter so  much crazier garo calls him heroic and  mentions the fact that it makes sense  that he was saitama student despite his  s-class ranking blast then uses a really  cool move called dimension cannon he  fires it off but garo sees fit to avoid  it as garo mentions it's a force  transfer aka i assume it would teleport  people to another place or dimension if  it touched them like kamui shuriken from  naruto but enough naruto references the  fight becomes like the dr strange film i  watched yesterday blast uses circular  portals to teleport garo from place to  place while delivering high speed  gravity punches it's definitely epic to  see what blast is finally capable of and  it is not disappointing finally it looks  like blast one he teleports garo away  but garo is progressing so fast he is  able to copy the ability and teleport  back he pretty much copies blast's moves  including his gravity punches blast uses  teleportation rings to protect himself  from the punches but eventually they  burst from the overload of energy and  blast is shocked to see it blast  realizes that if this much power keeps  being unleashed here the planet will die  he then decides he'll need to transfer  everyone else out which is the only  solution if garo can just come back  whenever he wants garo then talks big  first he praises blast saying that it  makes sense he's the number one s-class  hero which yeah he rocked but then he  says he's still not worth garo's  attention that's how strong garrow has  become at least in his own opinion i'm  sure blast has more abilities up his  sleeves but it definitely seems like  garo's got the advantage so far garo  ignores blast and then destroys genos to  bring out saitama's true strength it's  crazy and gets a lot darker than i  expected we appear to have a full black  page here which i'm guessing will be in  the official release too and it is a  nice touch to symbolize the gravity of  the moment it begins to rain probably  part rain part geno's liquids and  saitama is here we've never seen him  snap like this before garo points out  that saitama was too late to save his  friend garo passes saitama what used to  be genos core and we see a brutal image  of generous lifeless body that we're not  even gonna show for youtube reasons this  could be saitama's krillin getting  killed moment he just doesn't have the  hair to go super saiyan but otherwise  this could be crazy he remembers a  conversation with genos about hiro  timing and how he usually arrives too  late just like right now saitama thinks  to himself it sure doesn't look like he  has a hero's intuition and then we see  his serious face he launches a killer  series serious punch the expression the  gravity conveyed through the  illustration it's all amazing garo  copied saitama by entering saitama mode  and launching his own similar attack  blast the number one s-class hero who  was hyped for so long is now petrified  knowing that this energy will shatter  the earth if their fists collide and  that is the end of this epic chapter  arguably the best chapter of one punch  man ever we got blast getting serious  awakened garo getting serious even  saitama finally snapping and losing it  after watching his best friend get  destroyed right in front of his eyes by  garo the darkness in this one was  definitely unlike most one punch man  chapters so i really can't wait to see  what happens next what does a saitama  who has snapped and doesn't hold back  look like let me know your thoughts on  the chapter and what you expect to  happen in the next one it seems like  blast will have to get saita mangaro out  of this dimension and then the two can  go wild against each other and that will  probably be some of the best fighting  illustrations we've seen so far but for  now smash that like button with your own  serious punch if you enjoyed this review  and want to keep them coming you  definitely don't want to miss the next  chapter review which is looking to be  even crazier than this one with  saitama's serious power at full display  so subscribe and hit that notification  bell if you haven't so you don't miss  future one punch man chapter reviews and  updates while you wait for the next  chapter to drop feel free to check out  my one punch man playlist that includes  videos on all s class heroes dragon and  god level monsters and more link to that  is in the description and until next  time see ya space cowboys

